<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>

Explanation:
- The comment specifies that if the index is within the valid range (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the initial size of the vector), the result of setting the element at that index should be equal to the old value at that index.
- We use `\old(this.size())` to refer to the size of the vector before the method call.
- We use `\result` to refer to the return value of the method, which in this case is the old value at the specified index.
- We use `\old(this.get(index))` to refer to the value at the specified index before the method call.
